yoyo -p and piped stdin without --print now end stdout with exactly one newline. I ran it live before and after. Format, clippy and the full test suite all pass (6169 tests, 0 failures), and the work is committed as cf493152.

Before: from an empty temp dir with no config or extra flags, yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" | od -c gave P O N G \n \n. Piped stdin gave the same bytes.

Cause: neither newline came from the model. Both are yoyo's own end-of-turn writes in src/prompt.rs:
• one at the end of the event loop, if text was still being written (~l.1163);
• one closing the end-of-prompt step that prints usage (~l.102).

Fix: it's all in src/stream_leading_blank.rs, the filter both doors already pass through, so there's one copy of the rule and no second strip in prompt.rs.
• Once a line has ended after real text, any further whitespace is held back.
• If more text arrives, the held lines are written exactly as they were, so blank lines inside an answer (e.g. in a code block) don't change.
• If the turn ends, they are never written.
• No end-of-turn "finish" call is needed. That matters because both doors exit through std::process::exit on several error paths.
• The REPL, `--print, --output-format json/stream-json` and stderr are unchanged.

After, live: P O N G \n on both doors. A prompt asking for alpha, a blank line, then beta gave alpha\n\nbeta\n, so the blank line inside the answer was kept.

Tests:
• Two old expectations changed on purpose, with the old values kept in comments: the measured table row now expects "PONG\n", and one line in armed_filter_never_delays_content now expects "\n", followed by a check that the held line is written once text resumes.
• I also updated tests/print_stdout_contract.rs:626, which wasn't in the task's file list. It runs the real binary against a stub server and still asserted the old PONG\n\n ending, so the full suite failed until I changed it to one newline. The comment records the old value. Its name (…still_streams_model_leading_blank_lines) is now out of date; I didn't rename it.
• New full-string tables cover: ends with one newline (model with and without its own newline, \n\n\n, whitespace-only lines, CRLF, trailing spaces on the last line) and blank lines kept inside an answer (code block, blank line split across writes, indentation).
• The existing test that the unarmed filter (the REPL) leaves bytes unchanged still passes untouched.
• Positive control, run as one command: making the hold-back pass everything straight through failed 4 of the module's 7 tests by name. After restoring, all 7 passed and no NEUTERED marker was left.

Docs: updated docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md, which had stated the old PONG\n\n output, added a line to CHANGELOG.md under Unreleased, and added an ARCHITECTURE.md entry with the before/after bytes and the two prompt.rs lines. The module doc keeps the old "trailing newlines are byte-identical" sentence as a dated superseded claim; it still holds for --print and json output.

Limit: the final newline still comes from yoyo's end-of-turn write. If a door exits on an error before that write, output ends the way it did before this change, possibly without a newline.
